		"deviation": "None in count or ceiling: four authored rungs, the first four of the tool's eight, the other four the library's. Measured draw cost at the defaults: 14,152 / 5,960 / 1,748 / 820 against ceilings of 43,740 / 10,935 / 2,733 / 683 -- 0.32x, 0.55x, 0.64x and 1.20x, the last inside the free 1.5x because the panicle's stubs and the blade's fold are kept at rung 3 (dropping the stubs moved the silhouette a centimetre; flattening the fold moved the blades' coverage 0.33). Rung 0 spends 0.32x where the first revision spent 0.02x; an eight-column card at 0.49x was built first and bought nothing its 0.39 mm error target can see. WHERE THE RUNGS ARE DRAWN DEPARTS: the coverage claims (worst of 8 views, over the declared parameter range: 0.018 / 0.095 / 0.145) are converted by AgLod as a shrink, which places each rung further out than its band -- tools/rung-sheet.py reports it, and the silhouettes alone (0.0003 / 0.0048 / 0.0072) would land each rung inside its band.",
