  "source": "feedback/agoutline-leaf-ties-a-blades-base-to-its-apex-cba4b371.md: Betula pendula's leaf is deltoid -- broad, nearly truncate base, widest about 0.3 of the way up, a long acuminate apex -- and doubly serrate (alternate teeth cut to different depths, the character the genus is keyed on). Shape from that description and the flora; the author fits the points to the plate.",
