		"deviation": "TWO DEPARTURES, BOTH IN THE SAME DIRECTION AND BOTH FROM ONE FACT: THIS SUBJECT'S RUNG 0 IS FAR UNDER ITS CEILING.\n\n1. Rung 0 builds 2,734 triangles against a 16 px^2 ceiling of 43,740 and a photoreal allowance of 87,480 -- 0.06x, not 2x. It is not under-built: a fireweed is a rod, thirty-four thin blades and thirty small flowers with sky between all of it, and every one of those is a swept prism whose error against the real organ is already under the 0.39 mm target because the organ IS a swept form. The class prior of 25 px^2 per triangle assumes a subject whose surface is continuous; this one's triangles are large flat blades, so its measured triangle size is far above the prior (tools/ladder-audit.py --priors). A measured value outside the class range is a finding rather than a failure and it is recorded here: the `flower` class prior is set by dense subjects like plant/yellow-rattle (22,116 triangles at 0.30 m) and does not describe an open one.\n\n2. Because rung 0 anchors the slope, the coarser BUDGETS fall to 683, 170 and 42, and the rungs built are 902, 540 and 166 -- 1.3x, 3.2x and 4.0x. Against the ABSOLUTE 16 px^2 ceilings (10,935, 2,733 and 683) every one of them is comfortably under, at 0.08x, 0.20x and 0.24x. The ratio grows down the ladder because what a fireweed cannot go below is one triangle per organ and the organ count is a fact about the plant, not about the distance; the coarsest rung is where that floor bites hardest, and it is why rung 3's saving had to come from thinning the organ COUNT rather than from drawing each one more cheaply.\n\n3. WHERE THE RUNGS ARE ACTUALLY DRAWN IS NOT WHERE THIS TABLE PUTS THEM, and that is the honest statement of a gap the whole library has. `AgLod` derives a swap distance from the TIGHTEST BOUND A RUNG CLAIMS, which for this subject is always the coverage, so the four rungs swap at 0, 81, 182 and 216 m against a cull at 228 -- not at 0.3/1.7/3.4/6.7 m. The derivation assumes rungs far more faithful than a plant of separate thin organs can be made: a rung that loses a sixth of its projected area is one pixel wrong only at 81 m. Every generator in the library reads OVER on tools/ladder-audit.py for the same reason. It is declared, not papered over by claiming less error than was measured."
	}
}
