		"deviation": "ONE DEPARTURE AND IT IS THE RUNG COUNT: the size derives FOUR authored rungs and TWO are built. It is a measurement that contradicted the derivation, not a shortfall.\n\nFOUR WERE BUILT FIRST -- the shoot's own four rungs, fourteen times -- and their claims measured over five parameter points and two seeds:\n    asks the shoot for   triangles   silhouette   coverage\n      rung 1                12756      0.00045     0.15296\n      rung 2                 7560      0.00913     0.15320\n      rung 3                 2324      0.03205     0.13655\n\nTHE COVERAGE DOES NOT GROW DOWN THE LADDER AND AT THE COARSEST RUNG IT FALLS. A patch of fourteen shoots hides its own simplification: every shoot stands behind another, so what one of them stops drawing its neighbour is mostly still covering. At the default the three read 0.099, 0.149 and 0.065, and the coarsest is lowest because the shoot's two coarse moves pull opposite ways -- its raceme becomes one prism and over-covers, its leaves are thinned and widened and slightly under-cover -- and over fourteen overlapping shoots they nearly cancel.\n\nAgLod picks the cheapest rung whose every claim holds, so with honest claims the coarsest rung is both the most faithful in coverage and a sixth of the triangles, and everything between it and rung 0 is DOMINATED: never the cheapest acceptable rung at any distance, which AgConformance.its_rungs_differ would be right to refuse. Shipping four rungs would have been shipping two nobody draws. tools/ladder-audit.py reads COUNT on this subject and this paragraph is the answer to it.\n\nWHAT THE FINDING IS, stated generally because it is not about fireweed: a COMPOSITE OF N OVERLAPPING COPIES DOES NOT INHERIT ITS CHILD'S LADDER LENGTH. Overlap is the thing a ladder trades against, and a stand has already spent it. The same arithmetic says the patch could afford a coarser child than AgLod.child_rung will give it -- the shoot's rung 3 at 97 m departs 0.137 against rung 1's 0.153, for a sixth of the triangles -- and that saving of 10,432 triangles per instance is NOT taken here, because taking it means hand-picking a child rung. See gaps_expected: what is missing is a derivation that knows about overlap, and that is the core's to write.\n\nAGAINST THE CEILINGS, both built rungs are comfortable: rung 0 is 39,236 against a 16 px^2 ceiling of 43,740 and a photoreal allowance of 87,480 (0.90x, not 2x), and rung 1 is 12,756 against 10,935 (1.17x) or against the rung-0-anchored budget of 9,809 (1.30x)."
	}
}
␀␀␀␀␀␀# Sound credits

Every sound in transect is a field recording released under CC0 1.0
(public domain) -- no credit is required; it is given anyway. The cuts,
loops, levels and distance filtering are made by `tools/bake_sound.py`,
which lists where in each take they come from.

