		"deviation": "EVERY RUNG IS INSIDE THE 1.5x THAT PASSES WITHOUT COMMENT, and the previous version of this spec was not -- so this entry now records a departure that has been CLOSED as well as the one that remains.\n\nMEASURED, in DRAW COST (`AgGeom.Surface.draw_cost`: a cut-out triangle counts two, which is the unit `tools/ladder-audit.py` reads and the unit the budget is in), at the declared defaults:\n  r0  101,954 against 87,480   1.17x\n  r1   31,220 against 21,870   1.43x\n  r2    7,368 against  5,467   1.35x\n  r3    1,556 against  1,366   1.14x\n\nWHAT WAS HERE BEFORE: 177,660 / 47,964 / 15,324, which `tools/ladder-audit.py` read as 2.0x, 2.2x and 2.8x. The whole of that overspend was one number -- a compound leaf was 56 modelled triangles at the coarse rung a crown could afford, times 2,352 leaves -- and a leaf is now a card with its outline cut out, four triangles and eight in draw cost. THE SAVING WAS SPENT RATHER THAN BANKED: the crown gained a second-order branchlet between the branch and the shoot, which is the gap the previous version declared and did not build, and the crown's measured cover inside its own box went from a fan you could see through to 0.933 against the plate's 0.82-0.98 (a clean patch of the wall behind the tree reads 0.053 by the same instrument).\n\nAND THE CEILING ITSELF IS DIFFERENT, which is the second correction. The previous ladder was derived at a triangle size of 7.9 px^2 MEASURED OFF ITS OWN RUNG 0 -- so every rung 'fit' a ladder the generator had derived from its own overspend, while the audit read the same rungs at 2.0x to 2.8x of the class prior's. A measurement that moves the thing it is judged against cannot fail. The ceiling is the reference ladder's 16 px^2 and the measured size is recorded in `tri_area_measured_px2`, where it informs an estimate and gates nothing (the commission plugin's own fix, be7dd76).\n\nTHE REMAINING DEPARTURE IS RUNG 1's 1.43x and it is the wood's floor rather than the crown's: the bound stem filler `plant/birch-stem` has no rung below 36 triangles for an axis of any length, so 164 axes cost 5,904 whatever the distance. That is why the woody orders retire one per rung from rung 2 on."
	}
}
␀␀␀␀{
  "value": {
    "kingdom": "plant"
  },
  "source": "written for plant/agave (exp-20260927T160715Z-agave). The set held tree, shrub, herb, graminoid, fern, bryophyte and alga, and an Agave is none of them: it is not woody, so `shrub` and `tree` are false; `herb` -- `a non-woody vascular plant with stems and leaves` -- is false about the one thing a form is for, because it implies a soft, thin-leaved plant of herb size and this subject is a 3.7 m rosette of rigid water-storing leaves with no stem to speak of, whose whole mass IS its leaves. `bryophyte` exists in this vocabulary for exactly this reason: because `herb` would have been used otherwise.",
  "why": "a leaf- or stem-succulent: a vascular plant whose water-storing organs carry most of its mass, so its bulk and stiffness come from turgor rather than from wood"
}
