␀# THE LIBRARY THIS GAME IS BUILT AGAINST, pinned by commit.
#
# `tools/sync-library.sh` reads this and nothing else to decide what the
# library IS. A library improvement arrives here as a one-line change to
# `commit` and zero edits anywhere else -- if that is ever untrue, CHARTER G2
# is falsified and a `factory-feedback/` entry says why.
#
# `paths` is the library's RUNTIME: what a generator needs to build, with its
# suites removed. It is copied to the SAME `res://` paths the library uses,
# unmodified, because the library assumes it is the project root
# (`factory-feedback/the-library-assumes-it-is-the-project-root`).
#
# `requests` is the exception to "runtime": the library's requests TO this game
# (asset-generators `requests/`, one record each). They travel with the pin so
# the request and the library it belongs to arrive together; an entry answers
# one by citing `requests/<slug>.md` (`tools/feedback_entries.gd`), and
# `python3 tools/records/tools/board.py waits` lists what waits on this game.
#
# `evidence` is what the library's OWN guards recorded about those paths -- its
# committed fingerprint baseline. It is extracted under `.library/evidence/`,
# never onto a library path, and `test/suite_seam.gd` replays every row inside THIS
# project: a live build here must be byte-identical to what the library
# asserted about itself, or baked and live are not the same asset.
#
# Bump with:  tools/sync-library.sh --bump <commit>
repo=codestiff/asset-generators
commit=796e45a2d0465cad6906c2f96e79d947a078b992
paths=core generators taxa plates textures vocab requests fable-plans
evidence=test/fingerprints
␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀{
