			"date": "2026-09-28",
			"declared_by": "author",
			"multiple": 1.8,
			"reason": "A PHOTOREAL RUNG 0 OF AN AGGREGATE IS ITS PARTS AT THEIR OWN RUNG 0, and `AgLod.child_rung` says so: a pile rung 0 has error 0, so the distance it must hold is 0 and the cheapest child rung that holds it is the child's finest. Fourteen boulders at the clast's 20,480 triangles is 286,720 against a ceiling of 170,692. The clast has ALREADY been cut for this: its rung 0 is 0.12 of its OWN ceiling rather than the 0.48 one more subdivision would give, chosen so this multiple is under 2 and not 7. What would remove it entirely is placing the boulders as PARTS instead of welding them (`plans/032`), so each gets its own visibility range and only the two or three a viewer at half a metre can actually see are drawn at the finest rung -- that is the right fix and it is a different generator, recorded in the commission's gaps rather than half-done here (declared by the authoring session exp-20260928T214016Z-boulder-pile)."
		}
