 "_what": "THE PAGE'S SPLASH, A PRODUCT'S WORDS (docs/plans/226; page/splash.js draws it, tools/pack-web.py puts the built product's row in the page). title and gloss are the splash's words; notes_from names where the notes at the line's ticks come from, so they name what is really in the build: 'field_guide' reads the names in src/game/field_guide_words.json (what the valley grows and holds), shuffled a new way each day; 'coast' reads Norge's src/game/norge/coast.json, its sites and landmarks, in the order a course out from the hamlet meets them, with `soundings` between them. tap says what a tap leaves on the map.",
 "transect": {
  "title": "Transect",
  "gloss": "Into the wilderness: a night out in a Highland valley, grown on your device as you arrive.",
  "notes_from": "field_guide",
  "tap": "cairn"
 },
 "norge": {
  "title": "Norge",
  "gloss": "Tales of the North: a season on the coast, a boat, a ledger and the sea.",
  "notes_from": "coast",
  "soundings": ["12 fv", "8 fv, sand", "20 fv", "14 fv, rock", "tide rip"],
  "tap": "buoy"
 }
}
