ŒáOxg)€Íü^·Ûo‡ñÑIµÃ6uz>.3˜áÂ‹Õñ}LÜñì9ž#Áˆå`ÓphÁN«ñmqnµ'ÔÊâÙ›³¤µ¤çiÑ¡ã¬GïÀI¹Ã”à€rƒiÚæovAûó¿¿±þ&Öõ’ÜŠ&»d„	`;ÖÌìO±%ßîÀ$;spejáé{ÝhëL¶l|íÒ‰I{³¼	Å&Áˆe“¿ç½þÝý¾åUoÉþ·n¿o»ú4ár™÷Ä-Ð€<QËÝŒe«:º÷˜Eùß]ú&:ªË¿¯`â‡qp3||Fóc¢Dw½ÐÅ‹ÊUý"ÅÛ¨jÌ«øãÀ8•hW·û=ËÙ»ìòˆ%²4¥j¬Oº¼ b9CÏE£ðBÍÜíƒëN$\Ž¿È0 9Á¿-úÆ~@Ëž`MsÑA†ÌmxÜî‡Zb–œ ÆÏÈ“~¿“‚Éã7ìƒ»ÆmªFöï–éypm†®kÆnúBÛÀ·2ùfùûóoqvñ+ý÷)î¢+l¹) ·ÌÖâ¤¸/:’Ö¾ÿ6hûèãcŠPŒ]i—ð›1~ì—xô¹oH.ßç.N|¹ìÛÐ|à¦LŸü.5Æt‚Ãí°˜V¡müor»k90þî%E¼À7Yõ¬ïw3t+ûãÖî³ß1_ŽCwn=3ö"{”3e¦µÍåF­í'Î­ï©Œï’+½$]ä³?Ôô"uÀ‹8:6S9{]>î)øÏ~ôÿõÅy-é*þJ›5wÒó¬;^î_?l|¯òáø[ÏË¬“nri¾›}©ïÐµ/\çÓï¬+~—9°¿œ¦Ç|‘ô½×…_»!ä7ùGç_‚s©o¶N’Ã÷¸ÌßÞðþÑÒ7óhÿêyÃ½ÜŒæð¾ŸÜÆ_õ>;¯¬¿zq?:&—·_␀ÛI×'uhiÃ¬ï€6AºY¾|Ìý©>êšz¢\\½#;›Û×¢¼»÷¤¾␀|û§nºžö¦Å4X0m=C/{§óƒd¾¶|±Ó„ëS³ØöŽê9çá´1’ûvfþ3ûÕ"ß^ŸúæªüºYúê¾þ|»åÁ<*àÑ³ì?ãñ÷×·Òóä7åØï»¹s­SÓ^ÛAæïv˜èÁ¿ƒo&^cY×ïöêŽ¼?ôýü lU¾ú¿ãÇ³i‹ß2~l¡Š¯|¢çÄ?x¸?”ŸøÓþÎ¥}_ñ¦ó²¶zµ˜æFÁxOÈé=¿¿‰|ç0ÅY¯qog~ÕC´±.(c×;¦eÉÂ>Ãžå&à×¸=×ýãð´vŸ5ìbkanzÝ}¢yÑô‘·!7ÜD?·ÈÓf¢␀␀␀␀␀␀{
 "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
 "$id": "transect-walk/1",
 "title": "The walk's record, as the client posts it to the sessions Worker",
 "description": "THE SESSION RECORD'S SHAPE, delivery's side (docs/plans/161; dispatch row 83: the shape agreed between the delivery and edge sessions before either builds further). What TrWalkRecord.of and the DeliveryWalks autoload send to POST /v1/sessions (the library's ops/edge/README.md, 'The collector'): nothing outside these keys, so no identity key can reach the collector. test/suite_delivery.gd validates the client's records against this file. The edge's copy, when agreed, lives under the library's ops/edge/; until then this is the proposal it answers.",
 "type": "object",
 "required": ["record", "version", "build", "device", "walk", "ramp", "sitting"],
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "properties": {
  "record": {"const": "transect-walk", "description": "what this is"},
  "version": {"const": 1, "description": "this shape's version; a change of shape is a new version, refused by name by older readers"},
  "build": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "description": "the build stamp the start card shows: the build, the library pin and the commit (tools/pack-web.py), or 'transect <version> (unbuilt)'; the collector's one required field"},
  "profile": {"type": "string", "description": "TrProfile's name: web-review, native-desktop, native-mobile, native-desktop-4k"},
  "device": {"enum": ["phone", "tablet", "desktop"], "description": "the device's class only"},
  "viewport": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[0-9]+x[0-9]+$", "description": "the window's size in pixels, WxH"},
  "walk": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "the walk's id: when it set off, unix seconds (one walk, one row; a re-send of the same walk names the same id)"},
  "install": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{32}$", "description": "the install id: 16 random bytes in hex, made on the device's first run with diagnostics on, deleted from Settings; present only when diagnostics are on (docs/plans/160)"},
  "events": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "how many lines the walk's log holds"},
  "ramp": {"type": "array", "items": {"enum": ["inspect-credit", "end-card", "developer-mode"]}, "description": "the developer's doors this walk used (docs/plans/123)"},
  "participant": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^S[0-9]{2}$", "description": "a playtest stranger's id from the link (?p=S03), only in that shape"},
  "round": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$", "description": "a playtest round's name from the link (&round=strangers-1)"},
  "channel": {"enum": ["release", "candidate"], "description": "which build the walk was on: the release, or the candidate a player opted into from Settings, 'the next build' to players (docs/plans/186; dispatch row 107)"},
  "crash": {
   "type": "object",
   "description": "only when the page's watchdog stopped the walk (docs/plans/181; dispatch row 103): what stopped it and what was binding, in the page's own words and numbers, never the error's text",
   "required": ["cause", "phase", "idle_s", "binding"],
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "properties": {
    "cause": {"enum": ["oom", "abort", "frame-stall", "load-stall"], "description": "the engine's abort, out of memory, or the heartbeat silent for the watchdog's stall (src/delivery/watchdog.json)"},
    "phase": {"enum": ["loading", "playing"]},
    "idle_s": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "seconds since the last heartbeat"},
    "binding": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9 .,:/()%?-]{1,140}$", "description": "what was binding: the wasm heap and the device's memory, or the download's last progress line"},
    "heap_high_mb": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "the wasm heap's high-water mark, MB"},
    "js_heap_high_mb": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "description": "the JS heap's high-water mark, MB, where the browser tells (0 where not)"}
   }
  },
  "sitting": {
   "type": "object",
   "description": "a sitting of the playtest's record (docs/playtests/session-record.md), as tools/telemetry/sessions.py reads a collected one",
   "required": ["kind", "source", "at", "prompted", "reached_dusk", "nights_finished", "minutes", "marks"],
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "properties": {
    "kind": {"const": "home"},
    "source": {"const": "collector"},
    "at": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\\+00:00$", "description": "when the walk set off, UTC"},
    "prompted": {"type": "boolean", "description": "always false from the game (it cannot know); the facilitator corrects it"},
    "reached_dusk": {"type": "boolean"},
    "nights_finished": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0},
    "minutes": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "description": "the page's minutes so far"},
    "marks": {
     "type": "object",
     "additionalProperties": false,
     "properties": {
      "dusk": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0},
      "dawn": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0},
      "end": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0}
     },
     "description": "minutes from the page opening"
    },
    "ended": {"enum": ["dawn", "cold", "quit", "crash"], "description": "only when the walk is over; 'crash' when the page's watchdog stopped it (docs/plans/181)"}
   }
  }
 }
}
␀␀␀{
 "_what": "THE PAGE'S WATCHDOG (docs/plans/181; dispatch row 103, 'A crash is never a spinner'): what replaces the spinner and the bar with the crash card, and the card's words. page/watchdog.js reads these (tools/pack-web.py puts them in the page); test/suite_delivery.gd plays its states against them. A stall is the heartbeat silent for `stall_s` on a visible page: the download's progress while loading, the game's frame tick (src/delivery/walk_post.gd, TrHeartbeat) while playing. A page that was itself frozen (the watchdog's own check late by `frozen_s`) is not a stall: the clock starts again. THE DEVICE'S CARD (docs/plans/211; dispatch row 129): `need_mb` is what the walk needs of the device: the engine's static peak up the trail is 331 MB at every quality level (tools/bench.sh, docs/plans/211's table), with room; the quality ladder trades drawing, not memory, so there is one need until a profile holds less; page/memprobe.js grows a probe toward it in `probe_step_mb` steps before the engine is fetched, and `words.device` says what it needs and what the device gave.",
 "stall_s": 30,
 "check_s": 2,
 "frozen_s": 6,
 "tick_s": 1,
 "oom": "out of memory|cannot enlarge memory|array buffer allocation failed|\\boom\\b",
 "words": {
  "oom": "The game stopped. This device may be out of memory.",
  "abort": "The game stopped unexpectedly.",
  "frame-stall": "The game stopped. This device may be out of memory.",
  "load-stall": "The download stalled; check the connection.",
  "device": "This device could not give the game the memory it needs. The walk needs about {need} MB; {gave}. Our apologies. It plays in a desktop browser or on a recent phone. Copy the report and send it to us.",
  "device_gave": "this device gave {gave} MB",
  "device_silent": "this device would not say how much it can give"
 },
 "reload": "Reload",
 "copy": "Copy report",
 "need_mb": 384,
 "probe_step_mb": 64
