¼œ¦CTÿ(9jò}ç›Bßžò ýOVáu†-FÛI¯␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀{
 "_what": "THE FACED THING'S VERBS (docs/plans/180; the library's fable-plans/the-hud-has-one-verb rules 4 and 5, Transect's side of the dispatch's row 78; Norge's is src/game/norge/harbour_subjects.json): each thing the walker can face, its ONE Act (the button's label, TrCampActions.ROWS' word) and its short list (the other verbs, at most list_most). Every verb is a row of the action table with a rule, so no verb exists without one. ACT does the Act when it can be done now; when it cannot, the first of the list that can (a fire already burning: Light is refused, Feed is ACT's), and the list is the rest, each with its refusal. The tent is the model: Sleep, then Pack up, Look in, Bag in. The campfire gains a second verb: Feed, beside Light, so a laid fire is stocked before the match. Subjects with one verb have an empty list. camp_subjects.schema.json is its shape.",
 "list_most": 4,
 "subjects": {
  "deadwood": {"act": "gather", "list": []},
  "sticks": {"act": "gather", "list": []},
  "birch": {"act": "gather_birch", "list": []},
  "bramble": {"act": "pick_bramble", "list": []},
  "rowan": {"act": "pick_rowan", "list": []},
  "water": {"act": "drink", "list": []},
  "campfire": {"act": "light", "list": ["feed"]},
  "tent": {"act": "lie", "list": ["strike_tent", "look_inside", "bag_in_tent"]},
  "tarp": {"act": "lie", "list": ["stow_tarp"]},
  "bag": {"act": "lie", "list": ["stow_bag"]}
 }
}
