{
 "_what": "WHAT'S NEW, for players (docs/plans/025 step 4): written in plain words at each release -- drafted from the commits and the plans, approved by the owner -- newest first. Shown once after an update, and always from Settings.",
 "releases": [
  {
   "version": "0.1.7",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "Tucked into the corner",
   "lines": [
    "The action button, RUN, JUMP and the pack sit close together in the corner under your thumb, half the size of the cluster before, so the middle of the view stays clear.",
    "The buttons keep their size; only the gaps and margins around them shrank."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.6",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "Controls in reach",
   "lines": [
    "On a phone held sideways, JUMP, RUN and the pack sit close round the action button, in easy reach of your thumb, instead of across the middle of the view.",
    "The buttons are a comfortable size for a thumb and no bigger, so more of the valley shows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.5",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "Always something to do",
   "lines": [
    "How to play sets off late in the afternoon and always shows you the next thing to do, from the first armful of wood to lying down by the fire.",
    "The fire, lit when the evening comes, burns through the night on the wood you gathered: you're never sent back for more.",
    "Tap a plant and see what it is and that the open library grew it.",
    "The clouds drift at their own pace while the day goes by fast, and the sea loch is salt: drink from the stream."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.4",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "Enough for the night",
   "lines": [
    "How to play asks for enough wood for the whole night, then shows you when to feed the fire before it dies -- no more gathering, relighting and gathering again.",
    "How to play keeps the day's own pace: the afternoon is no longer hurried along.",
    "Your night is saved when you leave the page, and waits for you when you come back."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.3",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "Down to the sea loch",
   "lines": [
    "Walk down the glen to a sea loch: a beach, and a fishing station whose huts keep off the wind and the rain.",
    "How to play hurries the afternoon along, so the evening and its fire come sooner.",
    "The cold, the fire and the wet are retuned, so a careful first night can be lived through in any weather of the season.",
    "Smoother on phones: the ground ahead is built in the background, and the hares cost less when out of sight."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.2",
   "date": "2026-10-03",
   "title": "It keeps up with you",
   "lines": [
    "How to play keeps up with you: do things in your own order and it follows; let the fire die and it shows you the wood, feeding it, and lighting it again.",
    "Tap a tree (or click it) to see what it is -- How to play shows where.",
    "On a phone, the right thumb's buttons sit in an arc in reach, ACT's words above them; walk into a step and you hop up it.",
    "Smoother on phones: less work each frame as you walk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.1",
   "date": "2026-10-02",
   "title": "The whole night, shown",
   "lines": [
    "How to play is now a whole night: each thing to press lights up -- in your pack too -- and a light shows where to go, from the first wood to the dawn.",
    "Add Transect to your home screen and it opens full screen, like an app.",
    "The start screen has Feedback, and its Settings close again.",
    "The start screen and the pack fit a narrow phone.",
    "Transect has its own icon in your browser's tab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "version": "0.1.0",
   "date": "2026-10-02",
   "title": "Into the wilderness",
   "lines": [
    "A night out in a Highland valley: choose your pack, gather dead wood, lay and light a fire, eat, drink and get through to dawn.",
    "Or just explore: the same valley with no night to survive, time slowed, and the sky and the weather yours to turn.",
    "Choose your night -- the season, how lush, how many animals -- and a new valley grows for it, a different one each time.",
    "Your pack as pictures: tap what to carry. Pitch a tent or a tarp, lay out your bag, and sleep when you choose.",
    "Blackberries and rowan berries to pick, birch bark for tinder, and a stream to drink from.",
    "Mountain hares that bound away when you come near.",
    "Jump: Space on a keyboard, or JUMP by your right thumb on a phone. A heavy pack keeps you lower.",
    "Tap a plant or a hare to learn what it is; double-tap to look closer, and photograph it for your field notes.",
    "The sky as it is: the sun and moon for the date, cloud and rain, storms with thunder, and the northern lights.",
    "How to play: one short night that shows you how, then a quiet hint the first time anything new matters.",
    "Pounds or kilograms, Fahrenheit or Celsius: your device chooses first, Settings changes it. Phones start in battery saver.",
    "A Feedback button in Settings, to tell us what you think or what went wrong."
   ]
  }
 ]
}
