 "_what": "THE BUILD-TIME FLOORS (tools/bake_build_floors.py; docs/perf/card-priced-build-cap.md): per profile, per subject and rung (by name), the ms a unit of draw cost took to build at the pin below (`least` for a rung that pin's ladder lacked) -- the one the web profile's bench rows were measured at. TrRungCards prices a rung at the greater of its card's time and this times its draw cost, so a library speedup cannot by itself admit a finer rung. A profile or subject with no row is priced by its card alone. The rates are the reference machine's, as the cards' are, so every profile that builds on the device carries the same rows (the 4K desktop's too: docs/plans/107). Re-baked only when the phone has paid for it.",
